## ============================================================================
## VERSION HISTORY
## ============================================================================

VERSION_HISTORY:
  v2.1.22:
    date: "2026-07-23"
    title: "Pod round 2 — scene-as-cohort, teleprompter positioned in the free zone, mount jank removed (product owner staging feedback, afternoon)"
    changes:
      - "COHORT = WHOLE SCENE: buildPodCohorts (@ssi/core/pods/podCohorts.ts) now partitions the pod's sentence list one-cohort-per-scene_number run, replacing the morning's 2-3 sentence greedy turn-packing (which split an adjacency pair: a cohort ended on the question, the reply arrived next lap). POD_COHORT_MAX, turn-chaining and balanced-chunk splitting deleted. Missing scene_number rows (legacy cache) join the run in progress; all-null = one cohort. Pure partition, scene walls, per-cohort stage cohesion, min-drill lift, and the sentence-unit ratchet migration semantics all unchanged."
      - "TELEPROMPTER POSITION: PodTurnDisplay's top padding was a hardcoded 90px that under-shot the real header band (~96px + safe area), AND TeleprompterScroll's scrollCurrentIntoView measured current.offsetTop against the wrong origin — .teleprompter wasn't positioned, so offsets ran from PodTurnDisplay's absolutely-positioned, heavily-padded box, over-scrolling the current card clean under the belt pill. Fixed: .teleprompter is now position:relative (its own offsetParent), top padding = var(--header-total) + var(--hero-gap), bottom = var(--nav-total) + 2×hero-gap, and the anchor moved 0.33 → 0.5 (current line vertically centred in the free zone between top chrome and bottom controls — owner ruling; 0.33 was tuned against the broken full-screen container)."
      - "MOUNT JANK: card and text were always atomic in the DOM (verified frame-by-frame via headless probe) — the pop-in was positional: the first paint happened at scrollTop 0 (row low on the bare background), then the smooth corrective scroll visibly slid it ~400px into place. First anchor is now INSTANT (behavior:'auto', pre-paint in mounted+nextTick) so frame one is already in place; line-to-line changes stay smooth. A ResizeObserver re-anchors instantly through container resizes (e.g. the reminder-band padding collapsing when the transient fades — previously the rows drifted upward and stayed stranded until the next line change)."

  v2.1.21:
    date: "2026-07-23"
    title: "Pod-lap chrome cleanup — hero text pane hidden for the whole lap (one text surface rule)"
    changes:
      - "During ANY listening lap played through playPodLap (Layer-2 pod or Layer-1 cup), exactly ONE text surface may exist: PodTurnDisplay's TeleprompterScroll dialogue display (L2 only — L1 is audio-only), plus the one-shot transient pod-listening-reminder banner (~4s, then fades) and the small ambient listening dot. The entire hero-text-pane (hero-glass card, inline hint label, listening-pedagogy line, phase strip, guest Save-Progress nudge) is now v-show-gated on !playingPodLapAudio."
      - "Fixes the three-stacked-surfaces report (product owner, 2026-07-23, staging via the in-app preview triggers): (1) the hero-glass card rendered as an EMPTY white pill during sentence plays — all its inner branches were correctly suppressed but the card shell itself never hid, and it sat at z-index 10 ON TOP of the reminder banner; (2) the passive-listening 'like birdsong' pedagogy line filled the card as a big text panel whenever currentPodTurn was null (every lap's intro bookend; the whole lap in ?podview single-sentence previews between sentences); (3) both stacked with the grey reminder pill showing the same instruction."
      - "v-show (not v-if) because the pane's ResizeObserver (heroPaneBottom measurement for LegoAssembly clearance) binds to the element once at mount and must survive laps. The now-dead per-branch playingPodLapAudio guards inside the pane (hint label, listening-pedagogy, displayedKnownText stale-pill guard) were simplified away — suppression lives at the pane level."
      - "Main-cycle listening types (listen_intro / listening / listen_outro cycles, playingPodLapAudio=false) keep the pedagogy line in the hero card — unchanged. Preview-cheat note: ?podview composes each sentence as its own single-sentence lap, so the transient reminder re-fires per sentence and no build-up accumulation is shown — a preview artifact, not the real lap shape (nextLap plays sentences 1..N accumulating)."

  v2.1.20:
    date: "2026-07-14"
    title: "Kill Stage 0 in main-flow pods — replaced with an always-visible whole-turn LEGO-tile display, reusing the LegoAssembly engine (founders' decision, Tom + Aran)"
    changes:
      - "RETIRED: the Stage-0 audio-drilled per-atom breakdown ladder (explainer chunk-by-chunk -> pairs -> intention, ~5 reps) that used to prepend a pod sentence's first N views before its whole-sentence Stages 1-9. usePodLapScheduler.ts's nextLap() no longer weaves it in — every sentence now enters straight at Stage 1 on its first view. The main-flow agent-authored fusion-rung sub-ladder (the 'unified ladder', sentence.fusion_group) was removed alongside it for the same reason (it was Stage-0's newer replacement, same audio-drilling shape) — flattenPodRows() no longer computes fusion groups, and the atom_map_fine/window_known_map/takeg_audio_ids columns are no longer fetched by the scheduler. fusionDrill.ts itself (buildFusionGroups/buildFusionRungPlays/groupDepth) is UNTOUCHED and stays load-bearing for Listening Mode's Dialogues > Drill, via useListeningPods.ts — a fully separate, learner-opt-in surface this change never touches."
      - "REPLACED WITH: an ALWAYS-VISIBLE visual. During a main-flow pod lap, the whole dialogue TURN currently in play (one or more glued sentences, grouped by @ssi/core/pods' new computeTurnSpans/turnSpanForIndex over glue_to_next) stays on screen; each sentence lights up (is-active) as its PodPlay sounds. Under/within each sentence is a LEGO-tile breakdown — one tile per atom_map entry (kind atom/passthrough), its known-language gloss shown beneath, IN TARGET-SENTENCE ORDER — 'the visuals betray the target language grammar'. New component packages/player-vue/src/components/PodTurnDisplay.vue reuses LegoAssembly.vue directly (forced cycle-type='debut' so per-tile glosses always show, phase='voice2' so tiles assemble once and stay assembled — no reveal-gating) rather than building parallel UI; a scoped :deep() override repositions LegoAssembly's normally-fullscreen root to flow as one row among the turn's stacked sentences. Driven by the SAME PodPlay object driving the audio call (LearningPlayer's new currentPodPlay ref, set immediately before playPodSegment) — never a separate text lookup."
      - "No reveal-gating: unlike the 4-phase SPEAKING cycle's VOICE_2 rule (known text only until the second target voice), pod listening shows the tiled breakdown the whole time a sentence is in view — matches how Listening Mode's Dialogues teleprompter (ListeningOverlay.vue) already shows target+known text unconditionally. Speaking-mode pods keep their existing DECAY/reveal model in the main cycle (LegoAssembly's own prompt/voice1/voice2 phase-driven reveal) — separate concern, untouched."
      - "DELETED (dead once the runtime weaving was removed, verified zero other callers by grep before deleting): podStageComposition.ts's buildStage0Tier/composeSentenceArc/loadStage0ClipMaps, and stage0Sequence.ts's stage0ViewFor. KEPT: stage0Sequence.ts's lower-level sequencing (tierSequence/buildLadder/foldEventsToPlays/DEFAULT_STAGE0) and its atom-resolution types (AtomMapEntry/ResolvedAtom/resolveAtoms) — the admin-only Pod stage auditioner (/admin/pod-auditioner, PodStageAuditioner.vue) still calls these directly to preview/tune Stage-0 timing for content authoring; nothing about that tool changed. usePodLapScheduler's UsePodLapSchedulerOptions.stage0 option and useAlgorithmConfig's stage0Config plumbing into it were removed (LearningPlayer no longer passes stage0 to the scheduler); stage0Config itself stays in useAlgorithmConfig.ts for the auditioner."
      - "Every pod phrase remains a complete communicative unit with independent meaning ('good morning, Sarah', never 'good/morning/Sarah'; 'are you going to work?', never 'are you going/to work') — audio carries prosodic shape, the visual now carries grammar. Content-side segmentation enforcement (the rule + pod1) is being built in the dashboard repo in parallel; the app renders whatever segmentation it receives, unchanged by this pass."

  v2.1.19:
    date: "2026-07-14"
    title: "SEED playback simplified to the t-k-t-t sandwich, all @1x (listening cups + drained-eternal speaking review) — founders' decision (Tom + Aran)"
    changes:
      - "Layer-1 listening cups (useLayer1Scheduler.ts): DEFAULT_SEED_PLAYLIST dropped its trailing @2x stretch rep — the four-slot sandwich is now target(v1)@1x -> known@1x -> target(v2)@1x -> target(v1)@1x, ALL at 1.0x. Layer1SlotRole/Layer1PlayRole lost the t1x2/t2x2/ps2x speed-doubling members entirely (deleted, not defaulted-away) — a stale admin-config row still carrying them now silently drops that slot rather than throwing. Pod (Layer 2) speaking-mode decay and Listening-mode pods (drill/immersion) are UNCHANGED — this only touches SEED playback."
      - "SEEDS as full sentences in SPEAKING MODE once spaced-rep has drained (SEED_PHASE_START_OFFSET=144, reviewItemKind='seed' in generateLearningScript.ts): previously ran through the standard prompt/pause/voice1/voice2 production cycle (known -> silent pause -> target -> target). Now plays the SAME t-k-t-t @1x sandwich as the listening cups — a drained/eternal seed no longer needs an active-recall gap. Implemented as FOUR single-audio sub-cycles (emitSeedSandwich helper, shared by the main loop and the INF PLAY revival tail), mirroring the existing pod/listening single-audio-cycle trick rather than inventing a new phase machine. toSimpleRounds.ts and packages/core/src/script/playerTypes.ts (new Cycle.singleAudio flag) + SimplePlayer.ts's isSingleAudioCycle updated so these sub-cycles skip their empty phases silently instead of warning."
      - "Deleted dead pre-cups Layer-1 machinery in generateLearningScript.ts: ListeningConfig.l1ActiveSize/l1ReserveSize/l1UrnPullCount/layer1Playlist/layer1StagePlaylist/layer1StageDuration, emitL1Cluster, seedL1FireCount, graduatedQueue + l1Active/Reserve/RetiredSeedsList, createUrnSampler/reserveUrn/retiredUrn, layer1StageFor/layer1PlaylistForFireCount, the initialL1FireCounts param. All confirmed unreachable since the 2026-05-19 L1 main-flow removal (emitL1Cluster was defined but never called). Mirrored in useAlgorithmConfig.ts's ListeningModeConfig/DEFAULT_LISTENING. Deleted useListeningProgress.ts + @ssi/core's LegoListeningStore.ts (existed solely to hydrate the now-gone fire-count param) and their LearningPlayer.vue wiring (initializeListeningProgress, the dead l1_cluster_start/listening-cycle telemetry block keyed on emitL1Cluster's old uuid patterns, l1ClusterSeedsBumped). learner_l1_state DB table left alone — no migration, just stopped reading/writing it."
      - "Pod speaking-mode decay (usePodLapScheduler stage playlists) and Stage 0 / the fusion ladder are explicitly UNCHANGED — out of scope for this pass, per the founders' decision."

  v2.1.18:
    date: "2026-07-05"
    title: "Resume: reinstate narrow ceiling fallback — cursor null/unresolvable + populated ceiling no longer drops learners to round 1"
    changes:
      - "Blocker fix: the 2026-07-04 cursor-only sweep (v2.1.17) dropped the ceiling fallback entirely, which stranded live learners with last_completed_lego_id NULL but highest_completed_lego_id populated (e.g. a learner at S0002L02) at round 1 on resume. Reinstated narrowly: resolveStartLegoId, the cache fast-path, and the mid-session stale-matview repair block now fall back to highest_completed_lego_id ONLY when the cursor is null/unresolvable AND the ceiling is populated — read-only, never written back or ratcheted. Neither resolving still starts fresh at round 1, matching the pre-2026-07-04 behaviour these three sites had (see docs/position-and-ownership-model.md)."
      - "Extracted the shared decision (cursor → ceiling → null) to utils/resolveResumeAnchor.ts, unit-tested, and wired all three call sites through it instead of duplicated inline fallback logic."
      - "Infinite-play derivation (hasReachedInfinitePlay, cursor-only) is UNCHANGED by this fix — this is resume-position only, not the infplay predicate."

  v2.1.17:
    date: "2026-07-04"
    title: "Cursor-only position (phase 1) — infinite-play + resume derived from the cursor, not the ratcheted ceiling"
    changes:
      - "Cursor-only decision (docs/position-and-ownership-model.md): course_enrollments.last_completed_lego_id/last_completed_round_index (the cursor) is the ONLY position going forward. The ratcheted ceiling (highest_completed_lego_id/highest_completed_round_index, trigger ratchet_highest_completed_round) and current_mode are being retired via expand-contract; this phase repoints CLIENT READS only — no schema change, writes to the legacy fields continue for stale-PWA compatibility."
      - "Infinite-play is now DERIVED: hasReachedInfinitePlay (extracted to utils/infinitePlay.ts, unit-tested) — true iff no is_new LEGO remains beyond the CURSOR. Every call site (resolveStartLegoId's mode check, the instant-playback mode pre-check, the mid-session returning-user check) now passes the cursor (last_completed_lego_id), not the ratcheted ceiling or the stored current_mode column. Agrees with belt-skipped entries too: setMode's ratchetHighestTo write already stamps the cursor to the course's final LEGO on infplay entry."
      - "resolveStartLegoId and the cache-fast-path resume anchor DROP the 'fall back to the ceiling if the cursor isn't found' branch — resume is cursor-only, nothing else. An unresolvable cursor now starts fresh at round 1 instead of falling back to highest_completed_lego_id."
      - "useBeltProgress: fetchRemoteProgress reads last_completed_lego_id (not highest_completed_lego_id); mergeProgress adopts the remote cursor directly (no more Math.max ratchet merge) so a cursor moved back on another device is reflected here too; highestBeltIndex/highestLegoId no longer ratchet forward-only — they mirror the current cursor (setLastLegoId), so beltJourney's isComplete/isCurrent ticks (and CourseBrowser/PlayerContainer/SettingsScreen, which all read these refs) follow the cursor down as well as up."
      - "current_mode / infplay_round_index remain as WRITES only (setMode, bumpInfplayRound unchanged) — depth-into-infplay display still reads the infplay_round_index counter because the cursor is deliberately frozen at the ceiling during INF PLAY (persistCursorAtCurrentRound/persistLivePositionToDb skip writes in infplay mode); deriving depth from cursor round_index would require unfreezing that write path, deferred to a later phase (see repoint report)."
      - "App.vue / BrowseScreen.vue / CourseSelector.vue course-list cards (belt colour + 'N / total' position) now read last_completed_lego_id instead of highest_completed_lego_id. Admin useAdminUserDetail.ts / AdminUserDetail.vue prefer the cursor, falling back to the legacy ceiling only for rows that predate it."

  v2.1.16:
    date: "2026-06-08"
    title: "Cold-start instant-playback bootstrap + splash floor; welcome plays once EVER per learner; deleted-playback-module spec sync"
    changes:
      - "COLD START documented (new COLD_START section). INSTANT_PLAYBACK_ALL=true routes every course through useInstantPlayback.bootstrap() — round-map + first round's cycles in one parallel call so the first cycle plays in <2s with NO second roundtrip; localStorage-cached; prewarmInstantCaches(courseCode) warms on course switch (App.vue). The legacy upfront-load path (cached-script / generateScript+toSimpleRounds) is now only a catch fallback."
      - "Splash floor: loadingStage ref ('awakening'|'finding'|'preparing'|'ready'); MINIMUM_ANIMATION_MS is a DELIBERATE floor (300ms returning / 2800ms first-visit), run in Promise.all with loadAllData; ready = data loaded AND floor elapsed. Data now usually lands before the floor, so the floor is the gate."
      - "Belt + adaptation + listening hydration moved OFF the cold-start critical path: initializeBeltProgress/initializeAdaptationEngine/initializeListeningProgress fired via void Promise.all([...]) and NOT awaited (every consumer is null-safe with a default). Only getEnrollment (resume position) is on the critical path. Lazy overlay/modal chunks import-prewarmed on requestIdleCallback after ready."
      - "cold_start telemetry event added (logEvent) — the only event before tap_play; payload includes isFreshLoad (real load vs in-app course-switch remount), mountToReadyMs, nav-relative totalMs/mainExecMs/mountedMs (from window.__ssiBoot), animFloorMs, returnUser, guest."
      - "WELCOME now plays once EVER per LEARNER (course-agnostic) via learners.welcome_played_at, marked through service-role /api/welcome/played (api/welcome/played.ts: JWT-gated to own row, idempotent `.is('welcome_played_at', null)`). Was once-per-course on course_enrollments.welcome_played. localStorage 'ssi-welcome-heard' is the same-device fast path; hasPlayedWelcome() is the cross-device source of truth; guests fall through to localStorage."
      - "Spec sync to this session's @ssi/core deletions: useBeltLoader / playback PriorityRoundLoader island (SessionController/CyclePlayer/ThreadManager/RoundBuilder) and the AdaptationEngine class + WeightedSelector are DELETED. COMPOSABLES re-pointed: useInstantPlayback (loading) and useAdaptationEngine (composes kept MetricsTracker+SpikeDetector+MasteryStateMachine, getPauseMultiplier drives pause length). usePrebuiltNetworkIntegration + useLegoNetwork also deleted — constellation network is no longer populated at runtime (ensureNetworkInitialized is a no-op); NETWORK_INTEGRATION below is stale/aspirational, tracked by constellation-network.apml."

  v2.1.14:
    date: "2026-06-08"
    title: "Settings 'What's new' panel — scannable bullets, per-note Read more, note-derived update flag"
    changes:
      - "SettingsScreen 'What's new': restyled bullets (custom • markers, ~0.45rem spacing, 1.45 line-height) to read as a tidy list; each note's bullets collapse to the first 4 (BULLET_PREVIEW_COUNT) with a per-note Read more / Show less (state keyed by note.id, independent of the showAllNotes earlier-updates toggle); build-row 'Update available' badge now also fires on noteIndicatesNewer (latest note's released_at > build time +5min, SHA-equality short-circuits to 'current'), with an 'In the latest version' marker on the newest note."

  v2.1.5:
    date: "2026-06-04"
    title: "INF PLAY: complete the SR drain (≥89 rounds) + genuinely unbounded play"
    changes:
      - "Revival-tail FLOOR raised from a hard-coded 50 to max(spacedRepOffsets)+1 (=90). At 50 the final main-loop LEGO never received its N-55 / N-89 reviews — the last LEGOs were under-trained. The floor now guarantees the full N-1…N-89 spaced-rep drain completes for the final LEGO (methodology requirement). Floor derives from scriptShapeConfig.spacedRepOffsets, not a magic number (infPlayLookaheadFloor)."
      - "INF PLAY is now genuinely unbounded: expandScript() GROWS the revival lookahead by INF_PLAY_BATCH each expansion (a simple growing counter, infPlayLookahead), so the deterministic seeded stream keeps emitting new revival rounds (phase 1: the ≤89-round drain; phase 2 past the drain: pure random USE filling each ~22-cycle round). Previously the fixed 50 made expandScript a no-op in INF PLAY → dead-end at the tail."
      - "wrapInfPlayAtTail() retained as a SAFETY NET only (was the sole fix in the first cut): if a transient online generateScript failure returns 0 rounds, jump back to the first revival round instead of dropping to the paused summary — the auto-play analogue of advanceInfPlayRound's wrap. Growth is the primary path; the approaching-end watcher fires it ~5 rounds before the tail so play never reaches session_complete in the common case."
      - "Surfaced as 'stuck after a listening pod': the pod cadence lands a lap on the final revival round (lookahead was a multiple of the interval), so the old dead-end coincided with the end of a pod lap; only the bottom-nav forward (which already wraps) recovered."
      - "Continuation wired at onSessionComplete and the post-pod-lap branch in handleRoundBoundary: expandScript (growth) first, wrap as fallback. Offline still loops via appendCachedLoopForOffline (runs first), matching the partial-content 'straight to random, no drain' behaviour."
      - "Main-loop-boundary SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH (done): every divergent computation (infplayMainLoopCount ?? courseFinalLegoRef.roundIndex+1 ×6, roundMap.rounds[0].r-1 ×3, courseTotalRounds, the deterministic-build + regen generator counts) now routes through mainLoopBoundary() — the canonical /round-map (course_round_index) LEGO-ID-ordered map, held in its OWN stable ref (mainLoopMap), fetched once on load via getOrFetchRoundMap and never overwritten (unlike instantPlayback.roundMap, which bootstrapInfPlay clobbers with a synthetic infplay map). course_round_index is already the server-side authority (cursor-repair caps at MAX(round_index); course_stats.lego_count counts it)."
      - "infplayMainLoopCount ref DELETED. courseFinalLegoRef retained only for the final-LEGO id/seed (belt anchor, ratchet) + as a load-time fallback inside mainLoopBoundary() until the map resolves. mainLoopIndexForLegoId() gives main-loop position BY LEGO ID; handleRoundForward's INF-PLAY-entry test now reads position by LEGO ID, not the round array index. No counter up to the boundary; only infplayRoundIndex (per-round, in saveRoundProgress) counts PAST it. Also fixes a latent bug where the three roundMap.rounds[0].r-1 derivations mis-computed the boundary for deep (fromRound>1) infplay bootstraps."
      - "BEHAVIOUR NOTE for courses with unbuilt/no-audio LEGOs (e.g. German/Croatian): the round-map (is_new count) and the generator's PLAYABLE count can differ; the client now matches the server (round-map) instead of the generator's playable count. For fully-built courses the two agree exactly. Verify INF PLAY entry/boundary on a missing-audio course."

  v2.1.4:
    date: "2026-05-29"
    title: "INF PLAY deterministic online — frozen script run forward, no random fork"
    changes:
      - "Online INF PLAY now runs the SAME deterministic revival rounds the belts build (generateScript / generateLearningScript: ~50-round SR drain via SPACED_REP_OFFSETS out to finalLegoRound+89, then a SEEDED random-USE steady-state). No more random fork online."
      - "Random-USE tail is seeded-deterministic: generateLearningScript gained an `infplayRandom` param; LearningPlayer passes mulberry32 keyed on course+learner (makeInfPlayRng / hashStringToSeed). Same learner + position ⇒ same stream every session and regeneration, so back-nav returns to what was just heard. Main loop never consumes this param — main play unchanged."
      - "Resume directly INTO INF PLAY builds the local deterministic script and lands on the revival round keyed on infplay_round_index, instead of the per-session-random /infplay-cycles bootstrap (which survives only as a safety-net fallback)."
      - "enterInfPlayFromCache / appendCachedLoopForOffline (Math.random shuffle of cached cycles) demoted to OFFLINE-ONLY; called online it logs an error and refuses rather than shuffling."
      - "Stale main-loop handoffs (replaceQueueFromCurrent + tier-3 append) are now guarded by currentMode !== 'infplay' so an in-flight main-loop generateScript that resolves after the learner taps ∞ can't splice a LEGO-intro into the live INF-PLAY stream."
      - "No random encouragements / meta-commentary in INF PLAY: both the audio-commentary block and the visual-encouragement fallback in handleRoundBoundary are gated on currentMode !== 'infplay' (fixes back-nav pulling in the next encouragement)."

  v2.1.3:
    date: "2026-05-29"
    title: "Belt modal redesign (colour-only + ∞ activator) + round-advance in INF PLAY"
    changes:
      - "Belt modal belt row is now COLOUR-ONLY: dots with a thin black ring (1px rgba(0,0,0,0.55)), no text labels; belt NAME moved to title/aria-label. White belt now reads on the white modal."
      - "Added a glowing/throbbing ∞ INF-PLAY ACTIVATOR (.infplay-activator) at the end of the belt row — the deliberate entry point into INF PLAY (emit enterInfPlay → handleActivateInfPlay → enterInfPlay()). Distinct from belt dots; mist counterpart added (modal teleports to body, keyed :root[data-theme=\"mist\"])."
      - "handleRoundForward: WHILE IN INF PLAY, forward now ADVANCES through the revival rounds (advanceInfPlayRound) instead of being a no-op — rounds still exist in INF PLAY. Wraps at the tail, pins belt to final belt, bumps infplayRoundIndex. Round-back stays the INF-PLAY exit. Forward chevron no longer disabled in INF PLAY."

  v2.1.2:
    date: "2026-05-29"
    title: "Player nav remap — granularity = location"
    changes:
      - "Bottom-nav ‹ › now step the CYCLE axis (slot ±1, crossing round boundaries) via new SimplePlayer.stepCycle — previously round-level skip/revisit."
      - "Header ‹‹ ›› now ROUND/LEGO nav (handleRoundForward / handleRoundBack) — previously belt skips. Forward at the final LEGO enters INF PLAY; back replays the previous LEGO's debut (slot 0) and exits INF PLAY."
      - "Belt JUMPS are MODAL-only (central pill → handleSkipToBelt). The ∞ INF-PLAY indicator moved OFF the forward chevron ONTO the central belt pill (throbs, ∞ glyph, no progress line; mist counterpart added)."

  v2.1.1:
    date: "2026-05-26"
    title: "Encouragements = uncertain reward, between speaking rounds"
    changes:
      - "Commentary cadence is now a variable interval (~10 min of active play, ±30% jitter) instead of a fixed round count — an unpredictable reward that stays interesting. Measured in cycles played (not wall-clock) so long pauses don't trigger one on resume."
      - "Fires only at a boundary flanked by two speaking rounds with no pod lap — keeps a ~1-min encouragement away from listening and stops the double-audio (next-round intro overlapping a lap) on skip. Listening schedule unchanged."

